## Context: Errand failed because of distance, time or navigation; consumed acorn is lost.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.abort=§7The squirrel loses its way and gives up. The acorn is gone.
## Context: A frightened squirrel aborts its gift errand. The already accepted acorn is not returned.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.alarmed=§7The squirrel is frightened and drops the errand.
## Context: Squirrel returns and drops an item gift at the player feet.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.gift=§fThe squirrel scampers back and drops something at your feet.
## Context: Acorn is consumed, squirrel runs away to search for a gift before returning.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.accept=§fThe squirrel snatches the acorn and bolts into the undergrowth.
## Context: No standable away point could be found for the gift errand; acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.no_path=§7The squirrel sniffs the acorn, looks around, and stays. It has nowhere to run from here.
## Context: Squirrel is on its ten-minute gift cooldown; not a claim that it has eaten too much. Acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.full=§7The squirrel sniffs the acorn, but it is busy with its stash. Try again later.
## Context: A Guest (Harmony 0 to +9) has not yet earned Friend status (Harmony +10); acorn offer is refused and the item is kept.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.untrusted=§7The squirrel sniffs the acorn and watches you, but does not trust you yet.
## Context: An acorn offer is refused because the player's Harmony is below 0 (Uneasy, Shunned or Hated band); acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.squirrel.restless=§7The squirrel shies from your restless spirit.
## Context: Guidance ended unsuccessfully. Offering another acorn can resume toward the saved gift spot.
lothlorien.message.deer.abort=§7The white deer loses the way and lets you go. Another acorn may set it on its way again.
## Context: Leashing the deer during guidance ends the session; it is not killed or untamed.
lothlorien.message.deer.stop_leashed=§7The white deer is held on a lead and stops leading you.
## Context: Successful guidance ends and a plantable Great Mallorn nut is dropped in moss.
lothlorien.message.deer.gift=§fThe white deer stops and bows its head. Something glints in the moss: a Great Mallorn nut.
## Context: Guidance begins, acorn is consumed; instruct the player to follow the white deer.
lothlorien.message.deer.accept=§fThe white deer takes the acorn, lifts its head and turns. Follow it.
## Context: No navigable first waypoint toward an existing gift spot; acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.deer.no_path=§7The white deer looks around, but finds no way from here.
## Context: Guidance is refused while white deer is attached to a lead. Lead means the rope item, not leadership; acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.deer.leashed=§7The white deer will not lead while it is held on a lead.
## Context: No suitable gift destination in loaded Lothlorien terrain; acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.deer.no_spot=§7The white deer sniffs the acorn, looks around, and stays. It has nowhere to lead you from here.
## Context: Each white deer gives a Great Mallorn nut only once. It already gave its gift; offered acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.deer.gifted=§7The white deer nuzzles the acorn and lets it be. It has given its gift already.
## Context: White deer refuses guidance because the player's Harmony is below 0 (Uneasy, Shunned or Hated band); acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.deer.restless=§7The white deer shies from your restless spirit.
## Context: White deer gift guidance needs Friend status (Harmony +10), even though a Guest can approach the deer. Acorn is kept.
lothlorien.message.deer.untrusted=§7The white deer watches you, but does not trust you yet.
## Context: Tooltip line 3. Plant the nut on grass or dirt. Full tooltip also explains giant tree and space requirements.
lothlorien.message.nut.lore.plant=§7Plant on grass or dirt.
## Context: Tooltip line 2. Dimensions are Minecraft blocks: approximate width 40 and height 50. Full tooltip also explains giant tree and planting surface.
lothlorien.message.nut.lore.space=§7Needs space: about 40 wide, 50 high.
## Context: Tooltip line 1 of gifted Great Mallorn nut. Flet means wooden platform in the giant tree. Full tooltip explains tree size and planting surface.
lothlorien.message.nut.lore.tree=§7Grows a giant Mallorn with a platform.
## Context: Mounting refused: unicorn is bonded to a different player.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.other_owner=§7This unicorn is bonded to someone else.
## Context: Third accepted offer creates a permanent bond to this player; now rideable without a saddle.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.trust3=§fThe unicorn bows its horn to you. It is yours now; it needs no saddle.
## Context: Second accepted Elanor offer; flower consumed, trust stage 2 of 3.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.trust2=§fThe unicorn takes the elanor from your hand.
## Context: First accepted Elanor offer; flower consumed, trust stage 1 of 3.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.trust1=§fThe unicorn sniffs the elanor and watches you.
## Context: Less than ten seconds since previous offer; flower is kept. Turning over means examining, not rotating a block.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.wait=§7The unicorn is still turning the flower over. Give it a moment.
## Context: Unicorn is alarmed and refuses the offer; flower is kept.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.alarmed=§7The unicorn is too frightened to take anything.
## Context: Player lacks Friend status (is a Guest, Harmony 0 to +9); flower is kept.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.untrusted=§7The unicorn watches the flower, and you, but does not trust you yet.
## Context: Elanor offer refused because the player's Harmony is below 0 (Uneasy, Shunned or Hated band); flower is kept.
lothlorien.message.unicorn.restless=§7The unicorn shies from your restless spirit.
